These are separate from the unified audit table. Oracle writes .aud files into the adump directory (for example for SYSDBA connections). 
Nothing inside the database removes them by default, so they accumulate on disk. A Linux cron job handles it. 

crontab -e 
0 2 1,16 * * /usr/bin/find /u01/app/oracle/admin/DB/adump -type f -mtime +30 -name '*.aud' -exec rm -f {} ; >> /u01/aud_cleanup.log 2>&1 

cd /u01/ 

touch aud_cleanup.log 
chmod 755 aud_cleanup.log 

